{"resource": {"name": "T10 Vehicle Volumes", "id": "uzdg-5qcf", "parent_fxf": [], "description": "The City conducts transportation conducts, which counts the numbers of vehicles,\r\npedestrians, and bicycles moving through an intersection. Counts are typically\r\nconducted every 2 years during the weekday and weekend peak hours. The peak\r\nhours represents the time period where traffic counts are the highest due to worker\r\ncommute. Weekday counts are conducted at all City signalized intersections during the\r\nAM Peak Hours (7:00 A -9:00 AM) and PM peak hours (5:30 PM \u2013 7:30 PM) either on a\r\nTuesday, Wednesday, or Thursday in the Fall (when school is in session). Weekend\r\ncounts are conducted during the midday peak hour (1:00-5:00 PM) either on Saturday\r\nor Sunday in the Summer at signalized intersections in the Downtown and Main Street\r\nareas, as these areas tend to experience greater traffic as a result of the tourist/visitor\r\npopulation on the weekends", "attribution": "City of Santa Monica", "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2019-12-31T02:28:53.000Z", "createdAt": "2015-06-15T18:48:09.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2019-12-31T02:28:53.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2015-06-15T18:57:06.000Z", "columns_name": ["Santa Monica (PM Peak)", "Broadway (PM Peak)", "Centinela Avenue West (PM Peak)", "Ocean Park (AM Peak)", "Downtown Specific Plan Area IN (AM Peak)", "Colorado (AM Peak)", "Olympic (AM Peak)", "Pico  (AM Peak)", "Downtown Specific Plan Area OUT  (PM Peak)", "26th (AM Peak)", "Cloverfield (AM Peak)", "Year", "Santa Monica (AM Peak)", "Centinela Avenue East (AM Peak)", "Total PM Peak Vehicle Count", "Downtown Specific Plan Area OUT (AM Peak)", "Cloverfield (PM Peak)", "20th (PM Peak)", "Nielsen (AM Peak)", "Total AM Peak Vehicle Count", "Lincoln (AM Peak)", "20th  (AM Peak)", "4th Street (AM Peak)", "Main (AM Peak)", "Colorado (PM Peak)", "Olympic (PM Peak)", "Centinela Avenue East (PM Peak) ", "Wi